1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:04,500
Thirty-three years at the head of the most valuable company in the world...

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,310
and it ended in two weeks.

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:07,320
Because of a woman...

4
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:09,690
the Americans say was a spy.

5
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,600
This is Trend.

6
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:15,410
What is everyone talking about?

7
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:17,460
Jensen Huang. Founder of Nvidia,

8
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:21,160
the company that makes the chips all of artificial intelligence runs on.

9
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,210
On November 11,

10
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:26,900
the company's board accepted his resignation as CEO,

11
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,600
effective immediately. CFO Colette Kress took over as interim CEO.

12
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:31,990
How did the story begin?

13
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,570
On October 29,

14
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:40,930
the New York Times reported that US intelligence had concluded that a Chinese businesswoman,

15
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:42,210
named Alice Huang,

16
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:44,750
no relation to him,

17
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,450
was working for Chinese intelligence,

18
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:48,570
and had sought to get close to him.

19
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:52,820
The surprise? Alice was an executive at Megaspeed, a company in Singapore,

20
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,790
one of Nvidia's biggest customers in Asia,

21
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:59,590
which bought more than 4.8 billion dollars' worth of chips.

22
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:02,560
And that same company had already been suspected...

23
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,670
of smuggling chips into China.

24
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:06,570
Why did the story explode?

25
00:01:06,570 --> 00:01:08,710
Because Huang is no ordinary CEO.

26
00:01:08,710 --> 00:01:10,850
He's the man who meets presidents,

27
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:13,850
and lobbies Washington to allow chip sales to China.

28
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:17,740
And on November 8,

29
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:20,250
he sent his employees a letter admitting he had been unfaithful to his wife,

30
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,100
apologized,

31
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,490
and said he never knew the woman was a spy.

32
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:27,480
That same day,

33
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:29,660
the board opened an independent investigation.

34
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:34,670
A congressional committee summoned him to a closed-door session on November 18.

35
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:36,950
And the FBI is investigating.

36
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:37,810
As for China,

37
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:41,350
it called the accusations "baseless smears".

38
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:43,350
And what happened next?

39
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:47,610
The stock plunged. More than five percent on Monday.

40
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:49,440
Then, on Wednesday evening,

41
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:53,070
the Wall Street Journal reported the board was preparing to oust him,

42
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:56,490
and the company lost about another eight percent,

43
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:00,400
an estimated 340 billion dollars...

44
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:01,590
in hours.

45
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,130
And that same night,

46
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,490
came the resignation.

47
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:09,350
Even though the board said it had no evidence that any secrets were leaked.

48
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:12,810
A man who built the empire of artificial intelligence,

49
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,100
and fell in a story straight out of an old spy movie.

50
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:18,130
So was the resignation fair...

51
00:02:18,630 --> 00:02:20,350
or a punishment bigger than the mistake?

52
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:22,290
Tell me what you think in the comments.

53
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:24,500
Full sources in the video description.

54
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:26,810
Subscribe to the channel, and turn on the bell...

55
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,760
so you don't miss the next Trend.

